      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-11633",
      ":question/problem": "A class has $76$ students. Of the students, $35$ of them study mathematics, $26$ of them study physics. There are $12$ students that study mathematics and physics. Draw a Venn diagram representing this sample space. If a student is selected at random among the $76$ students, what is the probability that the student studies neither mathematics nor physics? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
