      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-87182",
      ":question/problem": "A physical education class has $42$ students. Of the students, $15$ of them practice basketball, and $19$ of them practice baseball. There are $6$ students that practice both basketball and baseball. Draw a Venn diagram representing this sample space. If a student is selected at random among the $42$ students, what is the probability that the student practices basketball but not baseball? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."
